{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And she lay with her father.</b> According to Rashi's interpretation, it implies that she did improperly. And if you ask: but we say in Bava Kamma, 'A person should always be first in a mitzvah' — for [Tamar's] advancing one night she advanced, etc. One may answer: she did well in that she was first, but in initiating the request for licentiousness and in teaching her sister, she did improperly." "<b>And she arose.</b> Pointed (with niqqud)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:59.848221285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}